WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:15.349
Hi, everyone! My name is Bobby and I'm a bird.

2
00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:21.117
I live on the back of a hippopotamus—a male hippopotamus, actually.

3
00:00:21.118 --> 00:00:25.289
His name is Henry.

4
00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:29.497
Henry and I live near a lake in Africa.

5
00:00:29.498 --> 00:00:34.143
Hippos live near rivers and lakes all over Africa.

6
00:00:34.144 --> 00:00:38.656
But they don't live on any other continent.

7
00:00:38.657 --> 00:00:43.749
How did a tiny bird and a big hippo become friends?

8
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:50.732
Well, we help each other out!

9
00:00:50.733 --> 00:00:54.513
I eat ticks and bugs off Henry's body.

10
00:00:54.514 --> 00:01:01.415
In return, he lets me live on his back.

11
00:01:01.416 --> 00:01:05.172
Hippos help other animals too.

12
00:01:05.173 --> 00:01:10.171
There are many plants around the rivers, swamps, and lakes.

13
00:01:10.172 --> 00:01:13.787
Henry makes a path through the thick plants.

14
00:01:13.788 --> 00:01:19.166
Then other animals can walk to the water.

15
00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:22.226
Henry also helps plants.

16
00:01:22.227 --> 00:01:28.906
Henry poops in the water, but it's okay.

17
00:01:28.907 --> 00:01:33.515
The plants grow strong from the nutrients in his poop.

18
00:01:33.516 --> 00:01:40.495
Other animals eat the plants and get strong.

19
00:01:40.496 --> 00:01:44.690
As you know, it gets extremely hot in Africa.

20
00:01:44.691 --> 00:01:49.696
Do you wear suntan lotion to protect your skin from the bright sun?

21
00:01:49.697 --> 00:01:54.835
Believe it or not, Henry makes his own suntan lotion!

22
00:01:54.836 --> 00:02:00.867
He sweats red oil.

23
00:02:00.868 --> 00:02:05.740
The oil prevents his skin from cracking or burning.

24
00:02:05.741 --> 00:02:10.521
I like to put some on my beak when I am hot!

25
00:02:10.522 --> 00:02:15.418
In ancient Greece, people thought hippos sweated blood.

26
00:02:15.419 --> 00:02:19.453
But I know it is just skin oil.

27
00:02:19.454 --> 00:02:22.844
Henry spends most of the day in the water.

28
00:02:22.845 --> 00:02:31.591
It's cooler there, and Henry's skin is especially suited to water.

29
00:02:31.592 --> 00:02:35.602
But Henry isn't a very good swimmer.

30
00:02:35.603 --> 00:02:41.115
He usually walks on the river or lake floor.

31
00:02:41.116 --> 00:02:47.583
Hippos' eyes, nostrils, and ears are on the tops of their heads.

32
00:02:47.584 --> 00:02:55.744
This helps them breathe and watch for danger when they are in the water.

33
00:02:55.745 --> 00:03:00.712
Henry can also stay underwater for five minutes.

34
00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:05.640
He closes his nostrils and presses his ears against his head.

35
00:03:05.641 --> 00:03:09.278
That way, water does not get in.

36
00:03:09.279 --> 00:03:15.603
When Henry comes out of the water, he makes funny snorts and hisses.

37
00:03:15.604 --> 00:03:21.076
It's hot now, but soon it will be evening.

38
00:03:21.077 --> 00:03:25.815
In the evening Henry and I leave the lake.

39
00:03:25.816 --> 00:03:29.045
Food is the reason Henry leaves the water.

40
00:03:29.046 --> 00:03:32.026
His appetite is huge!

41
00:03:32.027 --> 00:03:38.715
He can eat 35 to 45 kilograms of grass for dinner.

42
00:03:38.716 --> 00:03:44.249
Uh-oh! "Henry, are you going underwater again?

43
00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:48.806
I want to stay here longer!"

44
00:03:48.807 --> 00:03:54.499
When Henry goes underwater, I have to find a new place to rest.

45
00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.912
I would never argue with a hippo!

46
00:03:57.913 --> 00:04:06.487
Talk with you later. Good-bye!
